## Usage

### 1. Add the {{ .Name }} extension image to your Cluster

Define the extension under `postgresql.extensions` in your `Cluster` resource:

```yaml
apiVersion: postgresql.cnpg.io/v1
kind: Cluster
metadata:
  name: cluster-{{ .Name }}
spec:
  imageCatalogRef:
    apiGroup: postgresql.cnpg.io
    kind: ClusterImageCatalog
    name: postgresql-minimal-{{ .DefaultDistro }}
    major: {{ .DefaultVersion }}
  instances: 1

  storage:
    size: 1Gi

  postgresql:
    # TODO: Add required preload libraries and parameters from metadata.hcl.
    extensions:
    - name: {{ .Name }}
```

### 2. Enable the extension in a database

Create or update a `Database` resource to install the extension in `app`:

```yaml
apiVersion: postgresql.cnpg.io/v1
kind: Database
metadata:
  name: cluster-{{ .Name }}-app
spec:
  name: app
  owner: app
  cluster:
    name: cluster-{{ .Name }}
  extensions:
  - name: {{ replaceAll .Name "-" "_" }}
```

Alternatively, run the following SQL with the required privileges:

```sql
CREATE EXTENSION {{ replaceAll .Name "-" "_" }};
```

### 3. Verify installation

Connect to the database with `psql` and run:

```sql
\dx
```

You should see `{{ replaceAll .Name "-" "_" }}` listed among the installed extensions.

